From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenMCX <noreply@openmcx.invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pua: the P-CSCF's reg event subscription of TS 24.229 clause
 5.2.3

- The subscription is made "upon receipt of a 200 (OK) response to the first
  initial REGISTER request": a later REGISTER that finds the established
  record leaves it (it was refreshed at every REGISTER).
- "If continued subscription is required the P-CSCF shall automatically
  refresh the subscription": a reg event record has no end of its own, and
  every refresh asks for the Expires of the initial SUBSCRIBE (it asked for
  the time left to the first expiry).
- The refresh is sent "600 seconds before the expiration time if the initial
  subscription was for greater than 1200 seconds, or when half of the time
  has expired if the initial subscription was for 1200 seconds or less", from
  the duration granted (refresh_before until that is known).
- "If a SUBSCRIBE request to refresh a subscription fails with a non-481
  response, the P-CSCF shall still consider the original subscription valid
  for the duration of the most recently known "Expires" value": the record
  stays, no further refresh, and a new initial subscription follows its
  expiry (the record keeps its outbound proxy for it); no answer counts as
  such a failure. "Otherwise" (481) a new initial
  subscription at once, with the initial Expires, to the public user identity
  (it was made again after any error, for the time left plus 3 s, to the
  ended dialog's remote target).
---
